---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology — effiq"
  description="How effiq ranks model variants with domain scores, task costs, approximations, and efficiency rankings."
>
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-50 border-b border-border/80 bg-background/85 backdrop-blur-md">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5 no-underline">
        <span
          class="flex size-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary text-sm font-bold tracking-tight text-primary-foreground shadow-sm"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          eq
        </span>
        <span class="flex flex-col leading-none">
          <span class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">effiq</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground">
            efficiency × iq
          </span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <span class="ml-auto text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground">Methodology</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert">
    <p><a href="/" class="text-sm no-underline text-primary hover:underline">← Back to explorer</a></p>
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>effiq</strong> ranks model <strong>reasoning variants</strong> by capability per real or estimated task dollar.
      The default floor keeps the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index at 40 or more.
      You can change that floor and the metric weights in the explorer.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Artificial Analysis</strong></a>.
        Intelligence, coding, and agentic indexes. Measured cost per task. Throughput and time to first token.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://openrouter.ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>OpenRouter</strong></a>.
        Live provider prices, context length, and endpoint latency and throughput percentiles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://cursor.com/docs/models-and-pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Cursor</strong></a>.
        Subscription-pool variants, effort and thinking axes, and published token prices.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not run WhatLLM and LLM Stats adapters until robots and terms checks pass.
      Their derived scores never override Artificial Analysis or official provider prices.
    </p>

    <h2>Efficiency Score</h2>
    <p>For variants that pass the intelligence floor, the score follows these steps:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Percentile-rank intelligence, coding, agentic, and throughput.</li>
      <li>Log-normalize and invert task cost and latency.</li>
      <li>Combine with user weights. The default mix is 35/15/10/30/5/5.</li>
      <li>Apply evidence-coverage and approximation penalties.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The page also shows raw <em>capability per dollar</em> (domain score divided by task cost).
      That column stays separate. A near-zero price does not hide other ranking factors.
    </p>

    <h2>Usage profiles</h2>
    <p>
      Eight profiles change the domain evidence mix, the default weights, and the workload token assumptions.
      The profiles are General, Coding, Agents, Math and Science, Finance, Research, Writing and Literature, and Multimodal.
    </p>

    <h2>Approximations</h2>
    <p>Missing reasoning variants use this ladder:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Exact measured variant.</li>
      <li>Same-family interpolation between efforts.</li>
      <li>Nearest-effort extrapolation.</li>
      <li>Family aggregate plus effort curve.</li>
      <li>Insufficient data. No fabricated value.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Conservative ranking uses the less favorable bound of an estimate when confidence is limited.
      That bound is a higher cost or a lower capability.
      The UI keeps measured metrics and estimated metrics labeled.
    </p>

    <h2>Data freshness</h2>
    <p>
      A GitHub Actions workflow refreshes the matrix daily at 04:00 UTC.
      You can read freshness at
      <a href="/api/health">/api/health</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
